indows on the St. Charles side. Onto Coffee and beverages: They're simply awesome and amazing. I love that PJ's is the local folks. And no matter how awesome and inviting Starbucks is they are the National chain, and often get extremely busy so either as first and primary choice or a backup you can NEVER go wrong in here! The staff and baristas are friendly, warm, and amazing!!!!! It's a sin not to come on in and support the locals for the..."},{"business_id":"61vAJBC0E_fGjKDEYXJ2Zg","review_id":"l_kgjW1B248KTswiHiP1qg","date":"2018-01-14T01:42:55","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9091632962226868,"text_excerpt":"There are SO many of their shops everywhere around the French Market, and my friend and I were curious as to what they had to offer. As someone who is accustomed to the menu items off of Starbucks, I was quite confused at the selections they had. Granitas? Velvet ice?! What the heck are those! I asked the server at the counter and he openly admitted they were kind of competing items against the frappaccino at Starbuck's, and I wanted a cold drink so I got a blended mocha velvet ice. It was good, but my only gripe is that the ice separated too quick from the liquid within the beverage, so that at the end I was basically sucking on flavorless shards of ice. Overall a nice place to get more ..."},{"business_id":"61vAJBC0E_fGjKDEYXJ2Zg","review_id":"rv7Mgfx42g45FKndYNul2A","date":"2016-12-04T20:31:22","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.897022008895874,"text_excerpt":"Cute coffee shop located in the foyer of a hotel. It doesn't appear they offer all the bells and whistles of a full coffee shop but their standard fares met our needs. I purposefully inquired about chicory coffee, something I was told is a NOLA staple. I was told they were not offering it during the winter season but the staff member had a bag in the back that I was able to purchase."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"61vAJBC0E_fGjKDEYXJ2Zg","photo_id":"pbg-f5CYr_Y35wWtSWSfdw","label":"drink","im